keys-cipher-xchacha = XChaCha20-Poly1305
keys-cipher-cascade = Cascade XChaCha20 + AES
keys-cipher-info = All three are post-quantum: 256-bit keys. AES is the fastest. The cascade survives a break of one of the ciphers, at about half the speed.
keys-cipher-working = Re-encrypting…
keys-wipe = Overwrite files with zeros
keys-wipe-info = Every delete replaces the key and destroys the old one, so deleted data cannot be read. Zeros come on top; on flash memory they guarantee nothing by themselves.
